  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pursuant to Docket No. RP12-490</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">This amount represents the EDIT created by the reduction in the federal corporate income tax rate under TCJA, the decrease in the weighted marginal state income tax rate, and a state income tax adjustment associated with changes in ownership. The timing of the refund of the regulatory liability to rate payers is stated in the&#160;Docket No. RP22-1155 rate case settlement. Additionally, as of December 31, 2025, Northwest has $6 million of rate based deferred taxes established as a result of a decrease to the effective state income tax rate. This item will be subject to future discussions and negotiation with our customers in our next rate case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">This amount represents the EDIT created by the reduction in the federal corporate income tax rate under TCJA, the decrease in the weighted marginal state income tax rate, and a state income tax adjustment associated with changes in ownership. The timing of the refund of the regulatory liability to rate payers is stated in the&#160;Docket No. RP22-1155 rate case settlement.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pursuant to Section 14.12 of General Terms and Conditions of Northwest&#8217;s Tariff.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pursuant to Section 14.12 of General Terms and Conditions of Northwest&#8217;s Tariff</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The 25-year Evergreen incremental revenues and volumes are shown as separate line items although they fall under the TF-1 rate schedule.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas of Others Received for Transmission represents scheduled receipt nominations net of in-kind fuel. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled receipt nominations and actual physical receipts are captured in the 806 imbalances and are included in the numbers shown on lines 10 and 25 of page 520. The in-kind reimbursements are shown on lines 13 and 14.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Gas of Others Received for Contract Storage represents scheduled withdrawal nominations by others. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled storage withdrawal nominations and actual physical storage receipts onto the mainline are captured in the 806 imbalances shown on lines 10 and 25.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Northwest had the following storage quantities at 3/31/2026:</span>
      </div>
